{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Strengthen the seam test to assert `\"_UNTRACK_BATCH\" in init._untrack_runtime_markers_unit.__globals__` (name binding) rather than value membership.","criteria":["tests","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py:66: `assert init._UNTRACK_BATCH in init._untrack_runtime_markers_unit.__globals__.values()`","The stated contract is that the unit READS `_UNTRACK_BATCH` from its own module globals (so monkeypatch on init stays effective); value-membership does not assert the name binding — `init.py:410 _UNTRACK_BATCH = 200` could be renamed and any other 200-valued global would still satisfy the check."],"finding":"The new seam test's guard `init._UNTRACK_BATCH in init._untrack_runtime_markers_unit.__globals__.values()` is a value-membership check (does the int 200 appear among module globals), not a name-binding check. It neither proves the unit reads _UNTRACK_BATCH nor would it fail if _UNTRACK_BATCH were removed while another module-level int equal to 200 remained. It thus under-protects the very binding it documents (the reason the unit was kept in init.py).","id":"0","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py:66","norm_id":"n891aa27bfbaafef8","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Replace the value-membership assertion with `assert \"_UNTRACK_BATCH\" in init._untrack_runtime_markers_unit.__globals__` (and optionally that it `is init._UNTRACK_BATCH`).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na